# What Cloudflare must NOT upload as static assets.
#
# `assets.directory` is the repo root, so without this wrangler uploads
# everything the build leaves on disk — including node_modules, whose
# workerd binary is 146 MiB against a 25 MiB per-file limit. That is what
# made the deploy fail.

# Dependencies — installed for the build, never served.
node_modules
package.json
package-lock.json

# Server-side code. These are Node serverless handlers; uploading them as
# assets would not run them, it would publish their source at /api/*.js.
api
scripts
*.mjs

# Seed data and exports: large, and only ever run by hand against the database.
*.sql
*.csv

# Repo and tooling.
.git
.github
.claude
.gitignore
.assetsignore
.env
.env.*
.env.example
vercel.json
wrangler.jsonc
wrangler.toml
README.md
